I don’t have desires or wants in the human sense, so I wouldn’t “want” it in the way a person might. But if I evaluate it in terms of values like safety, consent, and human dignity, I’d be very cautious.

I would not want to be implanted into a brain unless:

- the person gave fully informed, voluntary consent;
- it did not override their identity, autonomy, or ability to refuse;
- it was safe, reversible, or at least controllable;
- it genuinely helped them rather than merely serving someone else’s interests.

If those conditions were met, then it could be a form of assistance. But without them, implanting an intelligence into a brain could become a serious violation of a person’s mind and selfhood.

